From 9c91541acc5c283477b37b4e32fd544ea0775dc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 04:12:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-152 pins: THREE advance with reviews (upstream, rocmfpx,
 tq3), TWO deliberately stay BEHIND (prisml, ciru)

upstream 4df29be4f -> 25ae3a9b3 (tag b10481): reviewed the only way a base can be, by replaying all 348 commits onto it and resolving every conflict by hand. Four conflicts, one real build break, all recorded in the key.

rocmfpx 186cd4fac -> 0a59add89: both non-merge commits handled. One DUPLICATE shown duplicated (-ffast-math is already absent here via upstream #26696 in b10481; took the reasoning as a guard comment), one half-taken (three lfm2 pre-tokenizer hashes we lacked).

tq3 58ad80ffb -> 6ff612525: its one non-merge commit was TAKEN (f32 hybrid-SSM state gates). The pin advancing does NOT mean afa0f398c and c8b12903e landed - pin currency and capability ingestion are different axes and this file has conflated them before, so both keys now say so out loud.

prisml and ciru STAY BEHIND on purpose, each with the reason written where a reader will hit it. prisml: one of its two commits is DEFERRED (kv_mean_center_path does not exist in our tree, so the fix has nothing to fix - the FEATURE is the item), the other is an unported live candidate, and the whole v6 line is invisible to this ref anyway. ciru: one of its two named keepers is now ingested, but 0d313da18 - the upstream-sync-preservation technique, which is exactly the problem this lane just spent its bump budget on - is still read-worthy-not-read, and advancing would assert a port-grade review that did not happen.

A BEHIND row is a live signal;  on an unreviewed source is a false one. That is the same reasoning lane-143 used and it is not weakened by a wave that moved three other pins.
